<title>FRANCE: French adj Sept current a/c surplus 14.2 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>French adj Sept current a/c surplus 14.2 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's current account showed a seasonally adjusted surplus of 14.16 billion francs in September, up from an unrevised surplus 10.40 billion in August, the Economy Ministry said on Friday.</p>
<p>The Ministry said that the seasonally adjusted surplus in the first nine months of 1996 was 83.93 billion francs, compared with a 64.43 billion surplus in the first 9 months of 1996  </p>
<p>Detailed figures in billions of francs showed:</p>
<p>					 Sept     Aug     Sept1995</p>
<p> Current account (adjusted)   14.16    10.40     2.94</p>
<p> Current account		  17.23     1.59     6.27</p>
<p> Merchandise trade		 3.14     4.41     2.60</p>
<p> Services			    7.45     5.77     6.49</p>
<p> Other goods and services	0.60     0.40     1.40</p>
<p> Income				0.37    -2.15     0.42</p>
<p> Transfers			   5.67    -6.83    -4.64</p>
